-- title:
--   Stability of the prime Hecke set under h↦ℓ̂ h⁻¹
-- statement:
--   Let $a,b\in\mathbb{Q}$ and let $\mathbb{H}=\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ be the associated quaternion algebra, let $\Lambda$ be an arbitrary $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule of $\mathbb{H}$, let $\ell$ be a prime, and let $h$ be a unit of $\mathbb{H}\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q},f}$, where $\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q},f}=\mathrm{FiniteAdeleRing}(\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}},\mathbb{Q})$. Write $\widehat{\Lambda}=\mathrm{finiteAdeleBox}\,\Lambda$ for the additive subgroup of $\mathbb{H}\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q},f}$ generated by the elements $z\otimes\alpha$ with $z\in\Lambda$ and $\alpha$ a finite adele all of whose components $\alpha_v$ lie in the valuation ring of the completion at $v$, and let $\mathcal{T}_\ell(\Lambda)$ be the set of units $h$ satisfying the four conditions $h\in\widehat{\Lambda}$, $\ell\cdot h^{-1}\in\widehat{\Lambda}$, $h^{-1}\notin\widehat{\Lambda}$ and $\ell^{-1}\cdot h\notin\widehat{\Lambda}$ (scalar multiplication by $\ell,\ell^{-1}\in\mathbb{Q}$). Let $\hat\ell$ denote the image under $\mathrm{finiteIdeleDiagonal}$ of the unit of $\mathbb{H}$ obtained from the unit $\ell$ of $\mathbb{Q}$ by the structure map, i.e. the diagonal idele $\ell\otimes 1$. The assertion is the equivalence $h\in\mathcal{T}_\ell(\Lambda)\iff \hat\ell\,h^{-1}\in\mathcal{T}_\ell(\Lambda)$. No hypothesis on $\Lambda$ beyond being a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule is required.
--
--   The involution $h\mapsto\hat\ell h^{-1}$ on the prime Hecke set at $\ell$ plays the role of the main involution on Hecke double cosets, and the lemma reconciles the two orientation conventions for it. It is used in the Čerednik–Drinfel'd class-set tower, where degrees of arrows in the coset graph and the existence of shift ideles are expressed through membership in $\mathcal{T}_\ell(\Lambda)$.
